<title>USA: Dura Automotive Systems Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Dura Automotive Systems Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>								 1996</p>
<p>					  1997    Actual  Pro Forma (a)</p>
<p> Revenues			     $  107,367 $  59,303  100,771</p>
<p> Cost of sales			    91,453    51,841   86,752</p>
<p>     Gross profit			 15,914     7,462   14,019</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>     administrative expenses	   7,228     3,864    6,733</p>
<p> Amortization expense			883	 262	829</p>
<p>     Operating income		    7,803     3,336    6,458</p>
<p> Interest expense, net		   1,896     1,089    2,217</p>
<p>Income before provision for</p>
<p>	   income taxes		    5,907     2,247    4,240</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	    2,363	 900    1,689</p>
<p>     Net income			    3,544     1,347    2,551</p>
<p>Net income per common and</p>
<p>	   common equivalent shares     0.40	0.27     0.29</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>	   and common equivalent</p>
<p>	   shares outstanding (b)	8,856     5,029    8,824</p>
<p>(a) Gives effect to the initial public offering and the acquisitions of KPI and VOFA as if they had occurred at the beginning of the periods presented.</p>
<p>(b) Weighted average number of shares outstanding on a pro forma basis was computed as if the initial public offering had been completed at the beginning of the first quarter of 1996. (Amounts in thousands except per share amounts -- unaudited)</p>
<p>		   ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
